---
import Layout from '../components/Layout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../config';

const contact = CONTACT_EMAIL.trim();
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="Who runs Evidence Stack, how to reach us, how corrections are handled, and how the site is paid for."
>
  <article>
    <div class="page-head">
      <h1>About</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Evidence Stack is an independent register of what is actually known about supplement
        claims. It sells nothing, reviews no brands, and carries no advertising, affiliate
        links or sponsorships. This page is the operator record: who runs it, how to reach
        them, and what happens when something here is wrong.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section>
      <h2>Who runs it</h2>
      <p>
        Evidence Stack is a non-commercial project operated from the European Union. Every
        compound page names its reviewer and the date of its last review; where a record still
        reads <i>"draft — unverified"</i>, it has not been through that review yet and says so
        rather than pretending otherwise.
      </p>
      <div class="pending">
        <div class="micro-label pending-label">NOT YET PUBLISHED</div>
        <p>
          The operator's legal name and correspondence address are not yet shown here. Until
          they are, treat this page as incomplete: an EU-operated site is normally expected to
          identify its operator.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      {contact ? (
        <p>
          Corrections, questions, and data-protection requests all go to
          <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a> — one address for all three.
        </p>
      ) : (
        <p>
          There is no contact address yet. Rather than print one that does not work, this page
          says so plainly: nothing sent anywhere would reach us today. An address will appear
          here, in the footer of every page, and in the corrections section of the
          <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a> as soon as it exists, and it will be the same
          address for corrections, questions and data-protection requests.
        </p>
      )}
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Corrections</h2>
      <p>
        A mis-cited study, a wrong sample size, a grade that doesn't survive contact with the
        literature — these are the reports worth making, and they are acted on rather than
        filed. Material changes appear in the affected claim's grade timeline, so a correction
        is visible to everyone, not just to whoever reported it. The full rules are in the
        <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>How it is paid for</h2>
      <p>
        Out of pocket. There are no ads, no sponsored records, no affiliate links, and no paid
        placement in the register — product records exist only to compute cost per gram and are
        facts from labels, not endorsements. If that ever changes, it changes on the
        <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a> page first.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Your data</h2>
      <p>
        The site sets no cookies and runs no analytics. The only personal data it handles is
        the email address of anyone who subscribes to regrade emails. What happens to it is in
        the <a href="/privacy/">privacy notice</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>What this site is not</h2>
      <p>
        A summary of published research, however careful, is not medical advice. A grade
        measures evidence, not what you should do — that depends on your health, your
        medication, and your priorities, none of which this site knows.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  article { max-width: 720px; padding: 32px 0 48px; }
  .page-head h1 { font-size: 28px; font-weight: 800; margin: 0 0 12px; }
  .lede { font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--body); text-wrap: pretty; }
  section { margin-top: 32px; }
  h2 { font-size: 18px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 10px; }
  p { font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--body); margin: 0 0 10px; }
  .pending {
    margin-top: 14px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--amber);
    background: var(--paper);
    padding: 12px 16px;
  }
  .pending-label { color: var(--amber); margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .pending p { font-size: 13px; margin: 0; }
</style>
